From ea3e7213955bfa1125b84ded987b0adee56c0ee3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:21:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] borg: mark the seen unique dead, not the race numbered like
 the record

borg_update_kill_old(i) has a fix-up for a monster whose race is a unique
the player has already killed: it marks that unique as dead in
borg_race_death[]. It indexed the table with i, the Borg's monster-record
index, instead of kill->r_idx, the race index, so it marked whichever race
happens to have the record's number as dead and left the seen unique
alone. The mark is never cleared during the session.

This is reached in normal play when a monster takes the shape of a killed
unique (a Maia of Aule can change into Quaker, Master of Earth). With the
record numbered 47, Grip, Farmer Maggot's Dog, still alive, was recorded
dead; the next unique scan dropped it from the living uniques, which
moved the depth the recall-depth decision in borg_recall() is based on.

Index the table with the race that was seen.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#94.
---
 src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c b/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c
index 0c347c5ad..b0f483ba4 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-flow-kill.c
@@ -345,7 +345,7 @@ static void borg_update_kill_old(int i)
      * around
      */
     if ((rf_has(r_ptr->flags, RF_UNIQUE)) && r_ptr->max_num == 0)
-        borg_race_death[i] = 1;
+        borg_race_death[kill->r_idx] = 1;
 
     /* We want to remember Morgy's panel */
     if (kill->r_idx == borg.id.morgoth) {
-- 
